Rem ==================================================================
Rem spiro.shoddy — the spirograph on screen.
Rem
Rem Run: mill run spiro.shoddy   (or ./build.sh — Git Bash/WSL on Windows)
Rem
Rem The window half. It reads the plan the core built and walks it with
Rem the turtle in one Fold: each step returns a NEW turtle carrying the
Rem line just drawn, and the last one is the finished picture. Nothing
Rem mutates — LOGO's REPEAT is Shoddy's Fold.
Rem
Rem There is no event loop. This is the "open, draw, return" shape:
Rem Main finishes once the drawing is blitted, and the window stays up
Rem until you close it. A program that has to react to keys or mice
Rem needs the scribbler's event loop instead.
Rem
Rem The window is why this runs under `mill run`: a woven
Rem `dotnet spiro.dll` has no window backend and stops with a message
Rem saying so.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "turtle.shoddy"
Include "spiro-core.shoddy"

Rem One step of the plan, drawn: ink the pen, go forward, turn. Each
Rem word hands back a turtle, so they nest left to right in the order
Rem the turtle actually moves.
Def Draw(t As Turtle, s As Step) As Turtle
    Let inked = SetPenColor(t, Red(s), Green(s), Blue(s))
    TurnRight(Forward(inked, Ahead(s)), Turn(s))

Def Main()
    Let start = Title(NewTurtle(640, 480), "Shoddy Spirograph")
    Let drawn = Fold(Plan(defaultSteps), start, Draw)
    Let shown = Blit(drawn)
    Print("drew " & Str(defaultSteps) & " steps - close the window to finish")
